{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The moose (North America) or elk (Eurasia), "Alces alces", is the largest extant species in the deer family.","title":"Moose"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Moose are distinguished by the broad, flat (or "palmate") antlers of the males; other members of the family have antlers with a dendritic ("twig-like") configuration.","title":"Moose"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Moose typically inhabit boreal forests and temperate broadleaf and mixed forests of the Northern Hemisphere in temperate to subarctic climates. Hunting and other human activities have caused a reduction in the size of the moose's range over time.","title":"Moose"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Moose have been reintroduced to some of their former habitats.","title":"Moose"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Currently, most moose are found in Canada, Alaska, New England, Fennoscandia, Baltic States, and Russia.","title":"Moose"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Their diet consists of both terrestrial and aquatic vegetation.","title":"Moose"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The most common moose predators are the gray wolf along with bears and humans. Unlike most other deer species, moose are solitary animals and do not form herds.","title":"Moose"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Although generally slow-moving and sedentary, moose can become aggressive and move quickly if angered or startled.","title":"Moose"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" Their mating season in the autumn features energetic fights between males competing for a female.","title":"Moose"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Dafeng () is a coastal district under the administration of Yancheng, Jiangsu province, China.","title":"Dafeng District"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Located on the Jiangsu North Plain with a coastline of 112 km , Dafeng was historically one of the largest salt-making areas in China and now is famed for its well preserved eco-system and numerous national conservation parks.","title":"Dafeng District"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The district has the largest national nature reserve for a rare deer species, Père David's Deer or Milu (麋鹿 ) in Chinese.","title":"Dafeng District"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It borders the prefecture-level city of Taizhou to the southwest.","title":"Dafeng District"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Europe, the Caucasus, Asia Minor, Iran, western and central Asia, the Atlas Mountains of north‑western Africa, and introduced populations in Australia, New Zealand, the United States, Canada, Peru, Uruguay, Chile and Argentina.
